Extract the reference subtitle once instead of demuxing the episode per subtitle

For an embedded track the plugin gives ffsubsync the video plus --reference-stream s:N, so
ffsubsync demuxes the whole file to pull that stream out. Measured on an 8.2 GB episode: 12.5 s
and 8218 MB read, repeated for every subtitle of that file - which is what made a ten-track
episode take minutes and look like it was analysing the same audio over and over.

The reference subtitle is now extracted once by the plugin's own container-index reader (29.5 ms,
0.1 MB), cached as <key>.ref.srt beside the speech cache, and passed to ffsubsync as a small SRT
(0.6 s, 6.5 MB). Later subtitles of the same file reuse it and report "Syncing (from cache)".

Output is unchanged: our reader and ffmpeg extract the same subtitles, and syncing against the
extracted file is byte-identical to syncing against the stream (both verified on the real file).
Extraction failure falls back to the previous behaviour instead of failing the sync. The fallback
demux is refused for reference extraction, since it would cost exactly what this avoids.

Checks: 127, ALL PASS (reference-subtitle specifier parsing included).

Version 1.1.0.34.
